diff --git a/docs/codex-fixed-account.md b/docs/codex-fixed-account.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..9ab74278
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/codex-fixed-account.md
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+# Fixed Codex account extension
+
+Local extension for the DSH GPT account panel, based on commit
+`ba200aefa0c657a3390f278e74a21708b3589a5c`. This is not an upstream CPA feature claim.
+
+`routing.codex-account` selects one stable `auth_index` from the Codex credentials.
+An empty value preserves existing routing; `paused` rejects new Codex requests.
+Any other value pins ordinary, streaming, and token-count execution to that
+account before retries. Missing, disabled, quota-limited, or failed accounts do
+not fall back to other accounts. Other providers retain their existing routing.
+Home dispatch is unsupported with this policy and fails closed.
+
+The selection is global to this CPA process and persists in its configuration.
+Requests already dispatched retain their captured account. Adding credentials
+does not change an existing fixed selection. Removing the selected credential
+must first pause the proxy; remaining credentials are not selected automatically.
+
+## Management contract
+
+These routes use existing CPA management authentication:
+
+- `GET /v0/management/routing/codex-account` returns `contract:
+  "codex-fixed-account/v1"`, `auth_index`, and `fixed`.
+- `PUT` at the same path accepts `{ "auth_index": "<index or paused>",
+  "expected": "<previous selection>" }`. The target must exist unless paused.
+  A stale expected selection returns 409. Configuration is persisted and reloaded
+  before success is returned. Empty targets are rejected; the panel cannot turn
+  rotation back on accidentally.
+- Inference requests may supply `X-CPA-Codex-Account` with their prepared account
+  identity. A different current selection returns 409 instead of delivering
+  account-scoped encrypted history to a newly selected account.
+
+OAuth login, credential listing/removal, and account-scoped quota retrieval use
+CPA's existing management endpoints. OAuth credentials remain owned by CPA.
+Known consumer: `dsh-gpt-compat-accounts` 0.1.0 in
+<https://github.com/linmu115/dsh-gpt-compat>, documented in `docs/accounts.md`.
+
+## Persistent localhost management credential
+
+`--local-management-password-file <private-file>` reads a nonempty password of
+at most 4096 bytes and makes it valid only for localhost management requests.
+The existing configured management password remains valid and unchanged.
+This option cannot be combined with the existing password flag.
+Restrict the file to its owning user and system services; never commit it.
+
+For ordinary server startup this file option does not activate the existing
+desktop controller's 10-second keep-alive shutdown. Existing password-flag and
+TUI behavior remain unchanged. Start future server instances with the same file
+option; launching without it will not accept the additional credential.
+
+## Verification and upgrade boundary
+
+Tests cover pinned execution, streaming failures, count failures, paused/missing
+accounts, stale prepared requests, and compare-and-swap configuration changes.
+This does not promise account safety or avoidance of service enforcement.
+Reapply and validate the extension when replacing CPA with an upstream build.
